From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 12:25:14 -0500
Subject: fix: the shield's and the moon's lit circle sits inside the row

The circle behind a lit shield or moon was the buttons' ink drop in its active
state: 26 DIP across in the 32 DIP row, 3 DIP from each edge, and as strong as
a press, 1.6:1 from a painted row. The owner saw it as too big and too bright.

A new base class, stedding::LitToolbarButton, paints the circle under the icon
instead: 20 DIP, 6 DIP from each edge, in the row's hover colour, 1.3:1 from a
painted row, one size and one colour for both buttons. The ink drop keeps its
press, which stays stronger than its hover (toolbar T44). Hover and press use
the same 20 DIP circle, so a hover over a lit button draws no second ring. The
icon stays on the circle's middle (toolbar T60; blocker Bk6; dark-pages Dk16).

Why: the owner, 2026-11-05, from a capture of the address row (BACKLOG S-423).

Removable when: never as behaviour.
